## 5. Architecture decision

### Mobile client

Use React Native with Expo and TypeScript in a new `mobile/` workspace inside the repository. Use Expo Router for file-based navigation and automatic deep-link routing, development builds for native integration testing, and EAS Build/Submit for signed iOS and Android delivery.

Reasons:

- The product team already works in React and TypeScript.
- One implementation can ship native Android and iOS applications.
- Expo provides maintained modules for secure storage, notifications, camera/media, linking, application metadata, and update delivery.
- Development builds retain access to custom native modules if the managed SDK is insufficient.

The exact Expo SDK and library versions must be selected from the current stable release when implementation begins and committed through the lockfile. SDK upgrades are deliberate work, not floating dependencies.

### Backend

Add a versioned API under `/api/mobile/v1`. Mobile endpoints return JSON only and never expose Inertia responses, redirects, flash messages, or HTML validation behavior.

Controllers remain thin. Existing policies, request rules, models, notification services, classifiers, media storage, and domain behavior should be reused or extracted into application services when web controllers currently contain the business logic. The web application and API must not implement competing rules.

Use Laravel API Resources for stable response shapes. Publish an OpenAPI document and generate the mobile TypeScript transport types/client from it. Backward-incompatible response changes require a new API version; additive fields remain compatible.

### High-level flow

```text
Expo mobile app
  -> HTTPS /api/mobile/v1
  -> authentication + rate limits + regulation/access gates
  -> API controllers
  -> shared application/domain services + policies
  -> Eloquent/MySQL + queues + media storage

Laravel domain events / UserNotificationService
  -> persisted in-app notification
  -> queued push notification outbox
  -> Expo/APNs/FCM delivery
  -> universal/app link
  -> Expo Router screen
```

